      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "During a deload, the nervous system temporarily takes a break from receiving intense, high-frequency stimulation, allowing the neural drive to recover and rebalance. This rebalancing process involves the concept of \"neural adaptation\", where weak motor neurons are strengthened, and strong ones are not overactivated, preparing to redistribute and increase overall neural drive upon return to challenging training. This congestion-unloading allows for an uncluttered neural system to optimize the activation of motor units, enabling more efficient recruitment during subsequent heavy training cycles.",
